{"kind":"panel","id":"0f9c4948-fbd5-42de-882b-bc7802bf08bd","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"The Footbridge","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[0,-300,520,220],"src":[],"text":"The Footbridge - lesson 8 of the Alpaca4d Playground.\n\nA C24 timber deck, 1.2 m wide and 120 mm deep, across 10 m, on a pin and a roller, with a herd of alpacas on it, 60 kg every metre. As built it bounces at 1.94 Hz, the pace of walking; the pier at mid-span makes it 7.75 Hz.\n\nCheck it by hand: f = pi / (2 L^2) x sqrt(EI / m), with EI = 1 814 kN m2 and m = 410 x 1.2 x 0.12 + 60 = 119 kg/m: 1.94 Hz for L = 10 m, four times that for 5 m.\n\nTry: unwire the pier from Assemble Model, make the deck deeper, or move Alpaca mass.","colour":[0,0,0,0]}
